{"id":"task-worktree-isolation-epic","display_id":null,"title":"Mandatory project-internal task git worktrees for write-producing TaskFlow work","description":"Establish VIDA framework and runtime law that every write-producing TaskFlow task executes in its own VIDA-managed git worktree inside the project root, default .vida/worktrees/<task-id>. Root checkout is control-plane only: bootstrap, planning, read-only diagnosis, dispatch, synthesis, and closure. Multi-session orchestration makes shared checkout writes unsafe because sessions can collide through dirty diffs, branch context, filesystem state, and merge authority. This epic defines task-owned project-internal worktree assignment before writer dispatch, explicit claim and lease binding, hard runtime gates for write packets without worktree evidence, merge or no-merge closure receipts, cleanup, diagnostics, and repo-hygiene protection so nested worktrees are never staged or committed.","status":"open","priority":0,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"1779463690978338300","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779463898844635000","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":null,"labels":["multi-session","protocol","runtime","taskflow","worktree"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"exclusive","order_bucket":"worktree-isolation","parallel_group":"worktree-isolation","conflict_domain":"framework-runtime-worktree-isolation"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":["crates/vida/src/**","docs/process/**","docs/product/spec/**","vida.config.yaml","vida/config/instructions/**"],"acceptance_targets":["Implementation tasks cover instructions spec config state CLI dispatch lifecycle merge diagnostics hygiene and release proof","Runtime design defines assignment claim binding merge gate cleanup diagnostics and repo hygiene behavior","Write-producing TaskFlow work requires project internal task worktree assignment before CL4 or writer dispatch"],