{"id":"taskflow-defect-next-lawful-closed-downstream-active-conflict","display_id":null,"title":"TaskFlow next-lawful blocks active task on closed downstream binding","description":"Discovered after closing taskflow-defect-next-lawful-continuation-source-drift on 2026-05-19. The task-close reconcile path leaves a downstream_dispatch_target binding for the closed task. \u000bida task next-lawful --json then reports runtime_taskflow_active_conflict against the live in_progress task \taskflow-defect-operator-surfaces-over-2s-read-model-projection. Expected behavior: a downstream closure binding for a closed task must not block the authoritative live TaskFlow active task; next-lawful should ignore/retire that closure handoff or let the active task be selected. This blocks full orchestrator+agents autonomy and reprioritization after defect closure.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779172822072432900","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779173316677600400","closed_at":"1779173316677600400","close_reason":"Fixed closed downstream closure marker conflict with active TaskFlow continuation; proofs and release install recorded in task notes.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"2026-05-19 fix evidence: second agentic defect wave after post-close diagnostic. Worker C changed `crates/vida/src/task_surface.rs`; Worker D added factual CLI regression in `crates/vida/tests/task_smoke.rs`. Behavior restored: a `downstream_dispatch_target`/`task_close_reconcile` marker for a closed task no longer blocks a different live `in_progress` TaskFlow task with `runtime_taskflow_active_conflict`; true open run_graph_task conflicts remain fail-closed. Proof: `cargo fmt -p vida --check`; `git diff --check`; `cargo test -p vida task_next_lawful -- --test-threads=1`; `cargo test -p vida --test task_smoke task_next_lawful_prefers_active_task_over_closed_downstream_closure_binding -- --nocapture --test-threads=