{"id":"taskflow-defect-next-lawful-closed-downstream-no-active","display_id":null,"title":"task next-lawful passes closed downstream closure binding when no active task exists","description":"After closing and consuming closure for \taskflow-defect-operator-surfaces-over-2s-read-model-projection, \u000bida task next-lawful --json returned status pass for closed task \taskflow-defect-next-lawful-closed-downstream-active-conflict via kind=downstream_dispatch_target, dispatch_target=closure, binding_source \task_close_reconcile. A closed downstream marker must never be a pass continuation when its task is closed, even if no other active task exists; it must be ignored as stale or fail closed so orchestrator+agents autonomy cannot re-enter closed work.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"defect","created_at":"1779175247704900500","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779176237332671000","closed_at":"1779176237332671000","close_reason":"Closed downstream continuation marker no longer passes when the bound task is closed and no active/ready successor exists; agent-backed proof and release install recorded.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"Closed by agent-backed fix on 2026-05-19.\n\nDefect shape:\n- After closing and consuming closure, `vida task next-lawful --json` could return `pass` for a closed task via `active_bounded_unit.kind=downstream_dispatch_target` / `binding_source=task_close_reconcile` when there was no other active task.\n- This violated autonomous orchestrator+agents task selection: closed work could become the next lawful continuation.\n\nFix:\n- `task_next_lawful_receipt` now treats a closed downstream marker as stale for selection and falls through to normal active/ready/no-ready logic.\n- Live downstream dispatch target binding still passes when the bound task is live.\n- Closed downstream marker with a different active task still defers to the active task.\n- Closed downstream marker with no active/ready task now blocks with `no_ready_task_candidates` instead of passing the closed task.\n\nAgent evidence:\n- Explorer confirmed the unsafe unit test encoded the defect and identified `task_next_lawful_receipt` as the minimal patch point.\n- Worker implemented the bounded patch and returned green targeted proof.\n\nProof:\n- `cargo fmt -p vida --check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `cargo test -p vida task_next_lawful -- --test-threads=1` => 17 unit/main pass, 3 task_smoke pass.\n- `cargo test -p vida --test task_smoke task_next_lawful_blocks_closed_downstream_closure_binding_without_active_or_ready_task -- --nocapture --test-threads=1`\n- `cargo test -p vida --test task_smoke task_next_lawful_prefers_active_task_over_closed_downstream_closure_binding -- --nocapture --test-threads=1`\n- `cargo build -p vida --release`\n- `target\\release\\vida.exe release install --skip-build --json`\n- SHA256 target/installed match: 8065EC1A27A9ADB31DC963402C6B1093C193267E4608F6BADC2D0F479D1FA5C2","labels":["agent-autonomy","continuation","defect","operator-surface","taskflow"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"exclusive","order_bucket":null,"parallel_group":null,"conflict_domain":"taskflow-next-lawful-continuation"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":["crates/vida/src/task_surface.rs","crates/vida/tests/task_smoke.rs"],"acceptance_targets":["closed downstream_dispatch_target bindings for closed tasks are not returned as pass when no active task exists","next-lawful falls through to ready/no-ready logic after stale closed downstream marker"],"proof_targets":["task_next_lawful unit regression","task_smoke factual closed downstream no-active regression"],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-defect-next-lawful-closed-downstream-no-active","depends_on_id":"taskflow-testing-defects-epic","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1779175247704900500","created_by":"vida task","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
{"id":"taskflow-defect-next-lawful-continuation-source-drift","display_id":null,"title":"TaskFlow next-lawful blocks on stale continuation source drift","description":"Discovered during autonomous orchestrator+agents testing on 2026-05-19. vida task next-lawful is blocked by continuation_source_drift: explicit binding points to runtime-codify-parent-child-closure-consistency-project while latest-run/status points to feature-clarify-spec-scope-root-users-pomaz-spec. Both task ids are missing from the authoritative backlog store. Expected behavior: next-lawful/status/graph-summary must ignore or retire stale continuation/run-graph bindings whose task_id is missing, then select a valid ready TaskFlow item or report a concrete actionable defect task. This blocks full orchestrator + agents autonomy and reprioritization.","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779171911885426200","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779172744264489000","closed_at":"1779172744264489000","close_reason":"Fixed stale continuation source drift in next-lawful via agentic bounded production/test lanes; proofs and release install recorded in task notes.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"2026-05-19 fix evidence: agentic execution used host worker lanes after canonical `vida agent-init --dispatch-packet ... --execute-dispatch --json` produced runtime lane receipt but downstream shaping remained blocked on pending spec/design gates. Worker A changed `crates/vida/src/task_surface.rs`; Worker B added factual CLI regression in `crates/vida/tests/task_smoke.rs`. Behavior restored: when explicit and latest-run continuation bindings disagree but both point to missing/stale task ids, `vida task next-lawful --json` no longer blocks with `continuation_source_drift`; it falls through to authoritative TaskFlow active/ready selection. If exactly one binding is live, the live binding wins; downstream dispatch target remains vali