{"id":"defect-operator-output-init-status-summary-too-large","display_id":null,"title":"Defect: routine vida init/status JSON output is excessively large","description":"Defect: routine VIDA operator JSON output is excessively large when the operator did not directly request a full/debug envelope.\n\nObserved evidence:\n- `vida orchestrator-init --json` produced ~66 KB / 1751 lines in normal re-entry flow.\n- `vida status --summary --json` produced ~103 KB because summary still includes heavy `host_agents` and `operator_session_projection` blocks.\n\nExpected behavior:\n- Routine operator/status/init surfaces must be compact and bounded.\n- Full nested envelopes are allowed only for explicit full/debug/direct long-output requests.\n\nInitial bounded scope:\n- Add/align compact summary behavior for init/status JSON surfaces.\n- Gate heavy nested blocks behind an explicit full/debug flag or remove them from summary view.\n- Add proof that summary output omits heavy keys and remains parseable.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"defect","created_at":"1779201043971200400","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779202035139008000","closed_at":"1779201515181978400","close_reason":"Fixed compact routine operator JSON output; full init envelope is explicit via --full; targeted tests passed.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"Post-close verification update:\n- Middle-oriented follow-up agent fixed stale status summary cache reuse by versioning the summary projection key to `status-summary-v2-latest` while preserving `status-full-latest`.\n- Release build passed through `vida release install --json`; first install attempt via environment-resolved `vida` hit Windows self-replace permission denial, then install succeeded using `target/debug/vida.exe release install --skip-build --source-binary target/release/vida.exe --json`.\n- Installed `vida` verification passed: `vida orchestrator-init --json` -> compact `view