{"id":"fix-session-identity-scoped-continuation-before-tui-service","display_id":null,"title":"Fix session identity and scoped continuation before TUI/service work","description":"Core runtime defect fix before TUI/service: canonicalize VIDA_SESSION_ID resolution, replace project-root fallback with per-session identity, and scope status/continuation/admission by current session plus claims. No TUI, daemon, service API, or dashboard implementation.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779350637912154500","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779350863651193400","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"# Development Packet: Session Identity + Scoped Continuation Before TUI/Service\n\n## Context\nThis task fixes the core runtime defect uncovered during pre-TUI/pre-service architecture analysis. VIDA already has a canonical multi-session design, but the current implementation still behaves like a project-global singleton in several places. Do not start Ratatui TUI, daemon/service install, service API transport, dashboard, or project activator wizard work in this task.\n\nCurrent observed live behavior on 2026-05-21:\n- `vida status --json.current_session.identity_source = stable_local_worktree_session_id`.\n- `vida status --json.current_session.session_id = local-worktree-*`.\n- `root_local_write_allowed = false`, `root_session_write_guard_status = blocked_by_default` for unrelated root-lane work.\n- `continuation_binding.active_bounded_unit = taskflow-case-18-rollout-regression-gate` globally blocks unrelated read/research/docflow shaping in the same worktree.\n- `claim_conflicts = []` and `global_blockers = []`, so the blocker is not a real resource collision; it is over-scoped continuation/session identity behavior.\n\nThe expected architecture is: one shared project truth store, multiple session-scoped controllers. Blocking authority must be scoped by current session, task/run, claim path set, conflict domain, and explicit global blocker class.\n\n## Canonical Specs And Docs\nPrimary spec:\n- `docs/product/spec/multi-orchestrator-session-ownership-and-claims-design.md:1`\n  - problem statement: lines 5-14\n  - identity model: lines 16-26\n  - claim/lease model: lines 27-53\n  - runtime status semantics: lines 54-71\n  - protocol updates: lines 72-81\n  - implementation work graph: lines 82-103\n  - proof targets: lines 104-112\n\nSupporting docs:\n- `docs/product/spec/authoritative-state-lock-recovery-design.md:32`\n  - concurrent read-only state access during dispatch wait is expected; do not solve this by widening locks or deleting lock files.\n- `docs/process/agent-system.md:6`\n  - host CLI systems are config-driven under `vida.config.yaml -> host_environment.systems`.\n  - host CLI execution posture must not depend on hardcoded vendor id heuristics.\n  - external/internal carriers are runtime adapters, not core identity law.\n- `docs/process/external-cli-carrier-operator-procedure.md:7`\n  - current external carrier family includes `hermes_cli`, `opencode_cli`, `kilo_cli`, `vibe_cli`, and `pi_cli`.\n  - Pi is one-process/one-dispatch and must not imply a long-lived host session.\n- `docs/process/project-development-packet-template-protocol.md:67`\n  - use bounded delivery task shape, explicit owned/read-only paths, proof target, and stop rules.\n\nExternal host identity evidence gathered during analysis:\n- Claude Code official env docs: `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars`\n  - `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is automatically set in Bash/PowerShell tool subprocesses and hook subprocesses to the current session id.\n  - `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID` exists for cloud/web sessions.\n- OpenCode CLI docs: `https://dev.opencode.ai/docs/cli/`\n  - OpenCode documents config env vars, but no stable ambient `OPENCODE_SESSION_ID` was found in official CLI env docs.\n- OpenCode sessions docs: `https://opencode.school/lessons/sessions/`\n  - one project can have many sessions; sessions persist and can be resumed.\n\n## Current Code Entry Points\nSession identity and owner evidence:\n- `crates/vida/src/orchestrator_session_surface.rs:61`\n  - `stable_local_session_id(state_dir)` currently derives fallback identity from `current_dir + state_dir`; this is the core defect.\n- `crates/vida/src/orchestrator_session_surface.rs:70`\n  - `current_session_id(state_dir)` currently checks `VIDA_ORCHESTRATOR_SESSION_ID`, `CODEX_SESSION_ID`, `CODEX_THREAD_ID`, then falls back to stable worktree id.\n- `crates/vida/src/orchestrator_session_surface.rs:397`\n  - `build_runtime_owner_evidence(...)` builds session evidence.\n- `crates/vida/src/orchestrator_session_surface.rs:429`\n  - `mutation_gate` currently becomes `blocked_live_other_orchestrator` for any live foreign session. This is too broad; foreign sessions are blockers only through claim/path/domain/global integrity rules.\n\nOperator projection and claims:\n- `crates/vida/src/operator_session_projection.rs:17`\n  - reads active claims and projects foreign runs/conflicts.\n- `crates/vida/src/operator_session_projection.rs:59`\n  - `claim_conflicts` are already path/domain/task/run aware, but the live-other owner gate can still block before this matters.\n- `crates/vida/src/state_store_orchestrator_claim.rs:66`\n  - `OrchestratorClaim` already contains the needed model: session id, task/run/lane, claim kind, paths, lease mode, status, blockers.\n- `crates/vida/src/state_store_orchestrator_claim.rs:236`\n  - `claim_conflict(...)` owns task/run/path/conflict-domain conflict logic.\n- `crates/vida/src/state_store_orchestrator_claim.rs:424`\n  - `acquire_orchestrator_claim(...)` is the correct write/admission conflict gate.\n\nGlobal latest run/status paths to scope:\n- `crates/vida/src/status_surface.rs:202`\n  - status currently calls `store.latest_run_graph_status()` globally.\n- `crates/vida/src/status_surface.rs:328`\n  - status currently calls `latest_explicit_run_graph_continuation_binding()` globally.\n- `crates/vida/src/state_store_run_graph_summary.rs:1563`\n  - `latest_explicit_run_graph_continuation_binding()` queries all explicit bindings globally.\n- `crates/vida/src/state_store_run_graph_summary.rs:1824`\n  - `latest_run_graph_status()` delegates to `latest_run_graph_run_id()` globally.\n- `crates/vida/src/state_store_run_graph_summary.rs:1831`\n  - `latest_run_graph_run_id()` selects newest execution plan row globally from `execution_plan_state`.\n\nTaskFlow admission/scheduler paths:\n- `crates/vida/src/taskflow_proxy.rs:2278`\n  - scheduler applies continuation dispatch gate when no current task is selected; the gate is built from global continuation evidence.\n- `crates/vida/src/taskflow_proxy.rs:2291`\n  - scheduler resolves current session via owner evidence.\n- `crates/vida/src/taskflow_proxy.rs:2299`\n  - scheduler filters claims from other sessions, which is good, but this only helps after session identity is correct.\n- `crates/vida/src/taskflow_proxy.rs:2710`\n  - `build_taskflow_next_decision(...)` applies global latest run/recovery/continuation gates.\n- `crates/vida/src/continuation_binding_summary.rs:289`\n  - continuation summary currently treats latest run evidence as the active bounded unit without session scoping.\n\nCLI/API surface likely touched:\n- `crates/vida/src/cli.rs:1201`\n  - `orchestrator-session` command args currently have no `--session-id` option.\n- Consider adding global or relevant-family `--session-id` with env `VIDA_SESSION_ID`, or centralizing resolution so all surfaces use the same identity resolver.\n\n## Required Design Decision\nIntroduce a canonical `VidaSessionIdentity` resolver and make all runtime status/continuation/admission surfaces consume it. Core VIDA must not hardcode host vendor session semantics beyond a configured alias/candidate list.\n\nRecommended resolver order:\n1. explicit service/session attach id if already available in caller context,\n2. `--session-id` CLI arg where supported,\n3. `VIDA_SESSION_ID`,\n4. `VIDA_ORCHESTRATOR_SESSION_ID` as backward-compatible legacy alias,\n5. host aliases from config/default registry:\n   - `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`,\n   - `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID`,\n   - `CODEX_SESSION_ID`,\n   - `CODEX_THREAD_ID`,\n6. generated per-session local VIDA token.\n\nThe fallback token must not be derived only from `(project_root, state_dir)`. It must represent the live host session/process/terminal instance. `project_root + state_dir` can identify `project_context_id` / `state_root_id`, not `session_id`.\n\nSuggested fallback behavior:\n- create/read a local session record under the existing orchestrator session store or a sibling session-token registry,\n- include `process_id`, `host_tool`, `started_at`, `last_heartbeat`, `project_root`, `state_dir`, and `worktree_environment_id`,\n- generate a stable token for the lifetime of the host process/session, not for every command if the same TUI/CLI session can persist it,\n- expose `identity_source = generated_local_session_token` or similar, not `stable_local_worktree_session_id`.\n\n## Required Behavior\n1. `VIDA_SESSION_ID` is the canonical session env.\n2. `VIDA_ORCHESTRATOR_SESSION_ID` remains supported as a compatibility alias.\n3. Host-specific ids are adapter aliases only; core status/claim logic consumes canonical `VidaSessionIdentity`.\n4. Different active host sessions in the same project/root must not collapse to the same id when host env is missing.\n5. `vida status --json` must split:\n   - `current_session`,\n   - `project_foreign_runs`,\n   - `project_foreign_blockers`,\n   - `global_blockers`,\n   - `claim_conflicts`.\n6. A foreign live session is not itself a global blocker.\n7. A foreign blocked run is visibility evidence, not a blocker, unless it shares task/run, intersects owned paths, shares exclusive conflict domain, or represents an explicit global state-integrity blocker.\n8. Observe/shared-read actions for status, research, docs inspection, and future TUI views must remain admissible while an unrelated write/delegated cycle is open in another session.\n9. Write/dispatch/proof operations must still fail closed on real claim conflicts.\n10. Global blockers remain global only for shared state integrity: schema migration, unreadable DB/state, lock corruption, root config mutation, or release-wide invariant protection.\n\n## Non-Goals\n- No Ratatui/TUI implementation.\n- No `vida service` daemon implementation.\n- No Windows/Linux/macOS service installation work.\n- No service API/IPC transport design beyond preserving a future session/request envelope.\n- No dashboard/web UI work.\n- No broad rewrite of TaskFlow scheduling beyond the session/claim scoping required for this defect.\n\n## Suggested Implementation Shape\n1. Add a small identity module or refactor `orchestrator_session_surface.rs`:\n   - `VidaSessionIdentity` struct,\n   - `resolve_vida_session_identity(state_dir, optional_cli_session_id, optional_host_config)`.\n2. Update `current_session_id(...)` and `current_session_record(...)` to use the resolver.\n3. Add `VIDA_SESSION_ID` precedence before legacy/vendor variables.\n4. Add tests proving fallback no longer returns `local-worktree-*` for missing host env.\n5. Replace broad `blocked_live_other_orchestrator` mutation gate with scoped projection semantics:\n   - keep live foreign sessions visible,\n   - only emit global blocker for actual global state-integrity blockers,\n   - rely on `orchestrator_claim` conflict detection for work collisions.\n6. Add session-scoped query helpers instead of global-only latest helpers, for example:\n   - `latest_run_graph_status_for_session(session_id)` or equivalent via active claims/owner evidence,\n   - `latest_explicit_run_graph_continuation_binding_for_session(session_id)`.\n7. Update `status_surface.rs` and `taskflow_proxy.rs` to use scoped helpers for current-session admission while still exposing global inventory separately.\n8. Preserve legacy ownerless compatibility but make it diagnostic/non-authoritative for unrelated current sessions.\n9. Ensure dispatch/claim creation records canonical `session_id` into claims and owner evidence.\n10. Keep JSON field compatibility where possible; add fields rather than removing existing ones unless tests prove old fields are wrong authority.\n\n## Acceptance Targets\n- `vida status --json.current_session.identity_source` reports `VIDA_SESSION_ID` when set.\n- `VIDA_ORCHESTRATOR_SESSION_ID` still works when `VIDA_SESSION_ID` is absent.\n- `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` and `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID` are recognized as host aliases when canonical VIDA env is absent.\n- `CODEX_SESSION_ID` and `CODEX_THREAD_ID` continue to work as host aliases.\n- Missing host env no longer collapses all clients in one worktree to `local-worktree-*`.\n- Two synthetic sessions in the same project root with disjoint tasks/paths can both read status and admit non-conflicting work.\n- A foreign session with a blocked unrelated run appears in `project_foreign_blockers` or equivalent visibility surface but does not block current-session ready/admissible work.\n- Same task/run conflict fails closed.\n- Intersecting owned path conflict fails closed.\n- Same exclusive conflict-domain conflict fails closed.\n- Global state-integrity blocker still blocks every session.\n- Existing root-session write guard semantics remain intact for root-local writes; this task must not grant local write authority accidentally.\n\n## Proof Targets\nMinimum targeted tests before closure:\n- `cargo test -p vida orchestrator_session -- --quiet --test-threads=1`\n- `cargo test -p vida operator_session_projection -- --quiet --test-threads=1`\n- `cargo test -p vida state_store_orchestrator_claim -- --quiet --test-threads=1`\n- `cargo test -p vida taskflow_next_decision -- --quiet --test-threads=1`\n- targeted status/scheduler tests covering two synthetic sessions in one temp state root.\n\nAdd or update tests to prove:\n- resolver precedence: `VIDA_SESSION_ID` > legacy alias > host alias > generated fallback,\n- generated fallback is per live session/process, not per worktree,\n- live foreign session alone is not a mutation blocker,\n- unrelated foreign blocked run does not force `latest_run_graph_status_blocked` for current session,\n- real claim conflicts still block admission,\n- status JSON preserves `current_session`, `project_foreign_runs`, `project_foreign_blockers`, `global_blockers`, and `claim_conflicts`.\n\nFinal proof before closing task:\n- `cargo fmt --check`\n- relevant targeted tests above\n- `cargo build -p vida --release`\n- install/refresh environment-resolved `vida` binary per project release procedure if this is normal runtime defect work\n- `rtk vida status --json` smoke check shows scoped session identity and no unrelated global blocker\n- `rtk vida docflow check --root . docs/product/spec/multi-orchestrator-session-ownership-and-claims-design.md` if docs/spec touched\n\n## Stop Rules\n- Stop and ask for architecture/escalation if scoping latest run by session requires a schema migration broader than `orchestrator_claim`/owner evidence can cover.\n- Stop if preserving legacy `latest_run_graph_status()` as a project-global diagnostic conflicts with current-session admission semantics.\n- Stop if a test requires granting root-local write authority; root-session write guard must remain separate from multi-session read/admission fixes.\n- Do not start TUI/service/dashboard work in this task.\n","labels":["defect","multi-session","pre-service","pre-tui","runtime"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"sequential","order_bucket":"multi-orch-session-fix","parallel_group":"multi-orch-session-fix","conflict_domain":"vida-runtime-session-identity"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":["crates/vida/src/cli.rs","crates/vida/src/continuation_binding_summary.rs","crates/vida/src/operator_session_projection.rs","crates/vida/src/orchestrator_session_surface.rs","crates/vida/src/state_store_orchestrator_claim.rs","crates/vida/src/state_store_run_graph_summary.rs","crates/vida/src/status_surface.rs","crates/vida/src/status_surface_truth_inputs.rs","crates/vida/src/taskflow_proxy.rs"],"acceptance_targets":["Fallback identity is per live session/process","VIDA_SESSION_ID is canonical and legacy/vendor aliases resolve through one identity resolver","foreign live/blocked sessions are visible but nonblocking unless task/run/path/domain/global blocker intersects","not project_root+state_dir","status/continuation/admission are scoped by current session and claim conflicts"],"proof_targets":["resolver precedence and fallback unit tests","same task/run/path/conflict-domain still fails closed","targeted cargo tests plus release build and status smoke","two synthetic sessions in one root with disjoint work do not block each other"],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"fix-session-identity-scoped-continuation-before-tui-service","depends_on_id":"feature-multi-orchestrator-session-scoped-ownership-clai","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1779350637912154500","created_by":"vida task","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
