{"id":"taskflow-defect-internal-fallback-activation-view-only-regression","display_id":null,"title":"Internal fallback dispatch still returns activation_view_only after route fallback selection","description":"Observed 2026-05-18 after fixing retry fallback ordering for run runtime-vida-taskflow-codex. Live continuation selected route fallback backend internal_subagents, proving the external fanout loop was repaired, but the internal handoff result blocked with internal_activation_view_only/tool_execution_failed: activation_kind activation_view, executes_packet=false, records_completion_receipt=false, receipt_backed=false. Evidence: packet .vida/data/state/runtime-consumption/dispatch-packets/runtime-vida-taskflow-codex-2026-05-18T06-21-38.4211942Z.json; result .vida/data/state/runtime-consumption/dispatch-results/runtime-vida-taskflow-codex-2026-05-18T06-22-04.5046458Z.json. Expected behavior: internal fallback carrier must either execute and record receipt-backed completion evidence or fail closed before handoff with actionable configured-template/carrier capability blocker; activation-view-only must not be treated as an execution attempt.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779085483231725700","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779317358393511000","closed_at":"1779317358393511000","close_reason":"activation-view-only-retry-fail-closed-fixed-with-focused-tests-release-install-and-closure","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"# Defect Audit: Internal Fallback activation_view_only — Validation & Correction Required\n\n**Audit Date:** 2026-05-21  \n**Scope:** Internal fallback dispatch, activation_view_only handling, receipt-backed completion  \n\n---\n\n## 🔴 Critical Defects (Need Fix Before Case Validation)\n\n### DEFECT 1: activation_view_only Treated as Retry Candidate — Contradicts Fail-Closed\n**Files:** `runtime_dispatch_execution.rs`, `taskflow_consume_resume.rs`  \n**Lines:** taskflow_consume_resume.rs:2608-2640  \n\n```rust\nfn retry_backend_for_dispatch_receipt(...) -> Option<String> {\n    let internal_timeout_like_blocker = matches!(\n        dispatch_receipt.blocker_code.as_deref(),\n        Some(\"internal_activation_view_only\") | Some(INTERNAL_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_WITHOUT_RECEIPT)\n    );\n    if internal_timeout_like_blocker {\n        // ← activation_view_only triggers retry path, NOT fail-closed\n        if let Some(packet_retry_backend) = ... { return Some(...); }\n        if let Some(fallback) = route_fallback.clone() { return Some(fallback); }\n        return None;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Problem:** System treats `internal_activation_view_only` as a transient failure that can be retried on alternate backend. Contradicts fail-closed principle: if internal carrier returns only activation view (no receipt-backed completion), retrying may produce identical results or cascade failures.\n\n**Severity:** HIGH — causes unnecessary dispatch churn and masks root cause.\n\n### DEFECT 2: Blocker Code Fallthrough to Generic Fallback\n**File:** `runtime_dispatch_state.rs`  \n**Lines:** 341-356  \n\n```rust\npub(crate) fn internal_host_activation_view_only_blocker_code(...) -> &'static str {\n    if prelaunch_blocker_condition { INTERNAL_CODEX_CARRIER_UNAVAILABLE }\n    else if terminal_blocker_condition { INTERNAL_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_WITHOUT_RECEIPT }\n    else { \"internal_activation_view_only\"  // ← generic fallback, no terminal enforcement\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Problem:** Third branch returns generic `\"internal_activation_view_only\"` string that is NOT checked by `is_internal_activation_view_without_receipt_blocker()` at runtime_dispatch_execution.rs:487 (which only checks the other two specific codes). Some activation_view_only results slip through without proper terminal handling.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 Medium Defects\n\n### DEFECT 5: Diagnostic Suppression for Non-Timeout Failures\n**File:** `runtime_dispatch_execution.rs`  \n**Lines:** ~1091-1094  \n\n```rust\nfn should_render_store_backed_activation_view_for_internal_failure(activation_only, success) -> bool {\n    !activation_only || success  // ← renders view when NOT activation_only OR when successful\n}\n```\n\nWhen `activation_only=true` AND `success=false`, returns false — no store-backed activation view rendered. Failure cases that are NOT timeout-related (e.g., carrier crashed, returned error) get only minimal default activation view with no diagnostic context.\n\n### DEFECT 6: mark_dispatch_result_execution_evidence Sets Conflicting Semantics\n**File:** `runtime_dispatch_execution.rs`  \n**Lines:** ~1670-1720  \n\nSets `view_only=false`, `executes_packet=true` on success path, but no guard preventing later code path from overwriting back to view_only=true (e.g., if error handler runs after this function).\n\n---\n\n## 🔵 Dead Code Identified\n\n### D1: Duplicate `configured_codex_cli_fallback_enabled`\n**Files:** `runtime_dispatch_execution.rs` (~line 1487) and `runtime_dispatch_state.rs` (~line 360+)  \nBoth define same function with identical logic. The one in runtime_dispatch_execution.rs is used internally; the one in runtime_dispatch_state.rs appears to be a copy never removed during refactoring.\n\n### D2: `internal_host_activation_view_only_requires_terminal_blocker` Narrow Applicability\n**File:** `runtime_dispatch_state.rs`  \n**Lines:** 330-339  \n\nOnly called from `internal_host_activation_view_only_blocker_code`. Single-use predicate that could be inlined. More importantly, checks `receipt_backed_completion_supported == Some(false)` — if config key is absent (None), returns false and falls through to generic `\"internal_activation_view_only\"` blocker code instead of terminal one. Silent configuration dependency that degrades blocker classification.\n\n### D3: `dispatch_result_activation_kind` Partial Coverage\n**File:** `runtime_dispatch_state.rs`  \n**Lines:** ~2010-2045  \n\nChecks three conditions for \"activation_view\" and two for \"execution_evidence\", but match is incomplete — if none met, returns None. Callers then fall back to defaults or skip classification entirely. Creates silent gaps in activation_kind tracking.\n\n---\n\n## 🔶 Inconsistencies\n\n### I1: Three Different Activation Kind Classification Code Paths\n1. `dispatch_result_activation_kind` (runtime_dispatch_state.rs) — checks result file for activation_kind field\n2. `activation_evidence_from_result_body` (runtime_dispatch_state.rs) — checks execution_evidence.status == \"recorded\" OR artifact_kind == \"runtime_dispatch_result\"  \n3. `receipt_result_path_has_execution_evidence` (runtime_dispatch_state.rs) — calls dispatch_result_activation_kind and checks for \"execution_evidence\"\n\nThese three functions can produce different results for same result file because they check different fields with different fallback logic.\n\n### I2: view_only vs activation_semantics.activation_kind Mismatch\nIn `default_activation_view`: `\"activation_kind\": \"activation_view\"` is explicit.  \nIn `build_fast_agent_init_packet_activation_payload`: uses `agent_init_activation_semantics()` which sets `\"view_only\": !args.execute_dispatch` but does NOT include `activation_kind`.\n\nDownstream consumers checking `activation_semantics.activation_kind` get None for fast-path results but \"activation_view\" for default_activation_view results.\n\n### I3: Retry Eligibility Contradicts Fail-Closed Intent\nAGENTS.md states: *\"If vida agent-init or runtime dispatch returns an activation_view_only handoff without execution evidence, treat that result as a non-executing bridge blocker\"*\n\nBut `retry_backend_for_dispatch_receipt` explicitly treats `internal_activation_view_only` as retry-eligible (taskflow_consume_resume.rs:2608+), directly contradicting fail-closed intent.\n\n### I4: Evidence State Label Identical to Blocker Code\n**File:** `runtime_dispatch_state.rs`  \n**Lines:** ~1606-1611  \n\n```rust\n\"activation_evidence_state\": if receipt_backed_execution_evidence { \"execution_evidence\" } else { \"activation_view_only\" }\n```\n\nUses `\"activation_view_only\"` as state label, identical to blocker code string. Creates ambiguity when parsing status reports — cannot distinguish \"evidence state is activation_view_only\" from \"blocker_code is internal_activation_view_only\".\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Search Criteria for Validation\n\n```bash\n# DEFECT 1: retry on activation_view_only\ngrep -rn 'internal_timeout_like_blocker\\|internal_activation_view_only' crates/vida/src/taskflow_consume_resume.rs | head -20\n\n# DEFECT 2: blocker code fallthrough  \ngrep -n \"internal_host_activation_view_only_blocker_code\\|is_internal_activation_view_without_receipt_blocker\" crates/vida/src/runtime_dispatch_state.rs\n\n# I1: three classification paths\ngrep -n \"dispatch_result_activation_kind\\|activation_evidence_from_result_body\\|receipt_result_path_has_execution_evidence\" crates/vida/src/runtime_dispatch_state.rs\n\n# DEFECT 5: diagnostic suppression\ngrep -A10 'should_render_store_backed_activation_view_for_internal_failure' crates/vida/src/runtime_dispatch_execution.rs | head -20\n\n# I3: retry vs fail-closed contradiction\ngrep -B5 -A10 'internal_timeout_like_blocker' crates/vida/src/taskflow_consume_resume.rs | head -40\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Recommended Fixes (Priority Order)\n\n1. **FIX 1:** Fail-Closed for activation_view_only — in `retry_backend_for_dispatch_receipt`, do NOT treat `internal_activation_view_only` or `INTERNAL_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_WITHOUT_RECEIPT` as retry-eligible: return None instead of fallback routing\n2. **FIX 2:** Consolidate Blocker Code Classification — ensure all three codes from `internal_host_activation_view_only_blocker_code()` are handled by same fail-closed path; remove generic fallback\n3. **FIX 4:** Add Diagnostic Context to Non-Timeout Failures — in `should_render_store_backed_activation_view_for_internal_failure`, render store-backed activation view for ALL failure modes, not just non-timeout ones\n4. **FIX 5:** Unify Activation Semantics Schema — ensure all code paths that produce activation_semantics include same fields (always include activation_kind)\n5. **FIX 6:** Separate Evidence State Label from Blocker Code — rename `\"activation_view_only\"` evidence state label to `\"evidence_state_activation_view\"`\n6. **FIX 3:** Remove duplicate `configured_codex_cli_fallback_enabled` — use canonical version from runtime_dispatch_state.rs\n\n---\n\n**Validation Gate:** Before validating this defect, fix DEFECT 1 (retry on activation_view_only). This is the most impactful defect — it directly contradicts fail-closed principle and causes unnecessary dispatch churn.\n","labels":["activation-view-only","agent-mode","internal-subagents","regression","runtime-dispatch","taskflow"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"sequential","order_bucket":"taskflow-testing-defects","parallel_group":null,"conflict_domain":"vida-runtime-dispatch"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":["crates/vida/src/runtime_dispatch_execution.rs","crates/vida/src/runtime_dispatch_state.rs","crates/vida/src/taskflow_consume_resume.rs"],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":["cargo-test-internal-activation-view-fail-closed","cargo-test-runtime-dispatch-state","vida-taskflow-recovery-status"],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-defect-internal-fallback-activation-view-only-regression","depends_on_id":"taskflow-testing-defects-epic","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1779085483231725700","created_by":"vida task","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
{"id":"taskflow-defect-internal-subagents-timeout-without-receipt","display_id":null,"title":"Internal subagents dispatch times out without receipt-backed completion","description":"Observed 2026-05-18 on live run runtime-vida-taskflow-codex after retry routing was corrected. The run now selects configured fallback backend internal_subagents, but vida taskflow consume continue blocks with runtime_dispatch_handoff_timeout; lane status records selected_backend=internal_subagents and blocker tool_execution_failed; dispatch result records blocker_code internal_dispatch_timeout_without_receipt with activation semantics view_only and no execution evidence. Expected: internal_subagents must either execute the packet and record receipt-backed completion evidence within the dispatch contract, or fail before handoff with a precise configured carrier/template/actionability blocker. The consume continue surface must preserve the actual run_id and actionable run/receipt context.","status":"paused","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779086984873576200","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779383796595447700","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"Paused under test-first runtime defect remediation on 2026-05-21. Resume only after failing activation/receipt contract test proves timeout or unavailable internal carrier cannot be treated as delegated completion.","labels":["agent-mode","internal-subagents","paused-for-test-first","receipt-backed","runtime-dispatch","taskflow","test-first-intake","timeout"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":null,"order_bucket":null,"parallel_group":null,"conflict_domain":null},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-defect-internal-subagents-timeout-without-receipt","depends_on_id":"taskflow-test-first-runtime-defect-remedia