{"id":"taskflow-defect-lane-supersede-stale-exception-metadata","display_id":null,"title":"Lane supersede can activate stale exception metadata for the wrong bounded unit","description":"Observed 2026-05-18 while recovering runtime-vida-taskflow-codex from internal_subagents timeout. vida taskflow recovery latest recommended vida lane supersede runtime-vida-taskflow-codex --receipt-id runtime-vida-taskflow-codex --json. The command exited 1 with open_delegated_cycle/tool_execution_failed but lane_status became lane_exception_takeover and exception_path_metadata.active_bounded_unit pointed to stale unrelated work: runtime-vida-taskflow-codex:graph-summary-pass-operator-contract-next-actions / PR #173. Expected: supersede must be atomic and bound to the current receipt/run/task/packet/session evidence; if metadata is stale or wrong-unit, it must refuse activation and record a precise blocker without changing takeover state.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779087072089283800","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779087796969573900","closed_at":"1779087796969573900","close_reason":"Fixed: lane supersede now validates receipt-bound exception metadata before mutation, rejects stale/missing/wrong-unit metadata with exit 2, and lane show exposes no root write scope unless metadata matches the active receipt. Focused tests passed and release install hash 84837B294E791E4B verified. Existing live lane_status was already mutated by the old binary but no longer grants write scope from stale metadata.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"2026-05-18 proof update:\n- Replanned defect order by criticality; this defect was selected as P0-1 because stale exception metadata can corrupt write authority and recovery sequencing.\n- Code fix in crates/vida/src/lane_surface.rs binds exception takeover metadata to run_id, dispatch_target, dispatch_packet_path, and source_exception_path_receipt_id.\n- `vida lane supersede` now validates receipt-bound metadata before mutating the dispatch receipt. Missing/stale/wrong-unit metadata fails closed with exit 2 before persist.\n- `lane show` no longer exposes root_local_write_allowed_for_only_these_paths unless metadata matches the active receipt summary.\n- Tests passed: cargo fmt -p vida --check; cargo test -p vida lane_supersede_activates_exception_takeover_for_recorded_exception_receipt; cargo test -p vida lane_supersede_rejects_stale_exception_metadata_without_mutation; cargo test -p vida build_lane_envelope_exposes_root_scope_only_for_active_takeover.\n- Release installed and PATH vida verified: C:\\Users\\pomaz\\AppData\\Local\\vida-stack\\current\\bin\\vida.exe hash 84837B294E791E4B.\n- Live proof: `vida lane supersede runtime-vida-taskflow-codex --receipt-id runtime-vida-taskflow-codex --json` now exits 2 with missing receipt-bound run_id on stale metadata and exposes zero root write scope. Existing lane_status remains lane_exception_takeover only because the old binary had already mutated it; current runtime no longer treats the stale metadata as write authority.\r\n","labels":["defect","exception-takeover","lane-supersede","operator-output","stale-metadata","taskflow"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":null,"order_bucket":null,"parallel_group":null,"conflict_domain":null},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-defect-lane-supersede-stale-exception-metadata","depends_on_id":"taskflow-testing-defects-epic","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1779087072089283800","created_by":"vida task","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
{"id":"taskflow-defect-legacy-codex-compatibility-surfaces","display_id":null,"title":"Legacy Codex compatibility surfaces still influence current runtime behavior","description":"Project invariant: active runtime behavior must be current-only and config/template/registry driven. Defect: Codex-era compatibility surfaces and aliases still influence current runtime/materialization/operator behavior instead of being limited to bounded artifact migration. Evidence areas include host runtime materialization that names codex-specific system layout, runtime dispatch fallback/activation-view-only compatibility handling, and mobile template drift where codex CLI model/tool defaults diverged from configured current carrier truth. Expected: legacy/codex compatibility may normalize old artifacts only with explicit evidence; it must not select carriers, shape dispatch commands, decide retry/rebind behavior, close tasks, or author operator output.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779086629619348000","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779104010239264900","closed_at":"1779104010239264900","close_reason":"Fixed first active Codex compatibility materialization surface: host runtime render label now derives from selected cli_system rather than hardcoded Codex. Proofs: format check; focused project activator materialization test; diff check; retired-label scan; release build; release install; fingerprint verified; operator warm latency proof recorded.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":null,"labels":["codex-compat","config-driven","current-only","legacy-removal","runtime-dispatch","taskflow"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":null,"order_bucket":null,"parallel_group":null,"conflict_domain":null},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-defect-legacy-codex-compatibility