{"id":"taskflow-defect-legacy-runtime-compatibility-paths","display_id":null,"title":"Runtime still contains active legacy compatibility paths instead of current-only implementation","description":"User rule recorded 2026-05-18: VIDA runtime must not keep active legacy code/functionality as execution behavior. Agent/runtime scan and live recovery exposed compatibility-shaped paths around legacy stale in-flight dispatch handling, legacy missing-first-receipt recovery, legacy internal_activation_view_only artifact interpretation, and compatibility aliases that can affect current TaskFlow execution. Expected behavior: current implementation owns the behavior directly through canonical config, templates, registries, runtime contracts, and state-store truth. Any old artifact migration may be bounded one-shot migration/normalization only, not an active branch that changes current routing, retry, closure, or dispatch semantics.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779086482423640600","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779101270837530800","closed_at":"1779101270837530800","close_reason":"Fixed current-only dispatch preview behavior: agent dispatch preview now uses current consume-bundle truth and fails closed when that truth cannot load; the smoke proof uses a project-bound runtime. Proofs: format check; focused dispatch-preview tests; source scan; diff check; release build; release install; fingerprint verified; operator warm latency proof recorded.","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"2026-05-18 Codex update: removed active legacy compatibility fallback from agent dispatch preview. \u000bida agent dispatch-next no longer substitutes \runtime_project_config_activation_bundle() from boot/migration compatibility rows when \build_taskflow_consume_bundle_payload fails; it now fails closed on current consume-bundle truth. The alignment smoke test now runs from a project-bound runtime instead 