{"id":"taskflow-defect-operator-surfaces-over-5s-architectural-rewrite","display_id":null,"title":"Vida operator surfaces over 5 seconds require architectural rewrite","description":"User rule recorded 2026-05-18: any vida operator operation that takes more than 5 seconds must be architecturally rewritten, not treated as acceptable latency or solved by increasing timeout. Evidence in current session: vida doctor --json took about 7.6s; live vida agent-init --dispatch-packet ... --execute-dispatch --json fast-block path still took about 5.6s even though no nested carrier was launched. Expected: normal inspection/planning/status/recovery/dispatch-gate operator surfaces complete within the project latency budget; slow command families must be analyzed at state-store/lock/IO/graph/reconciliation boundaries and refactored to bounded, cached, or incremental execution with explicit proof.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1779088613512228100","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1779090780302154500","closed_at":"1779090780302149900","close_reason":null,"source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"Hard-ceiling latency fix applied. Architecture: runtime-consption latest snapshot lookup no longer parses every historical final snapshot; it iterates newest-first candidates and returns on first admissible match. Existing fast paths kept: task ready snapshot read and agent-init packet activation without store. Proof: cargo fmt -p vida --check; cargo test -p vida runtime_consumption_state -- --nocapture; cargo build -p vida --release; release install fingerprint C3EDF190EE78AEB4F1ABE7D7688A5EE5D6EC96D2C23B30F9852C975C5F98B358. Installed serial measurements after install: task-ready 845ms, status-json-summary 3150ms, status-json 3072ms, doctor-json 3356ms, orchestrator-init 4026ms, agent-init-no-execute 220ms, agent-init-execute-prelaunch-block 3916ms. No measured normal surface remains over the 5s hard ce