{"id":"taskflow-defect-orchestrator-init-json-timeout-envelope","display_id":null,"title":"Orchestrator-init JSON timeout envelope","description":"Found during taskflow-case-bootstrap-orchestrator-init: vida orchestrator-init --json exits with plain text timeout 'Timed out building taskflow consume bundle...' instead of a machine-readable release-1 operator envelope with status, blocker_codes, next_actions, and artifact_refs. Expected by AGENTS re-entry, codex-agent-configuration-guide runtime hardening, orchestrator-runtime-contract-hardening-design, and TaskFlow proof-runbook JSON operator contract.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"defect","created_at":"1778675651296689300","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1778676364453321700","closed_at":"1778676364453321700","close_reason":"fixed orchestrator-init --json timeout envelope: timeout branch now emits release-1 JSON operator contract with blocked status, taskflow_consume_bundle_timeout blocker, next actions, artifact refs, operator_contracts, and shared_fields; targeted tests, release build/install/fingerprint, and live JSON proof passed","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"Defect evidence\n\n- Found in `taskflow-case-bootstrap-orchestrator-init`.\n- Repro before fix: `vida orchestrator-init --json` exited with plain text `Timed out building taskflow consume bundle for vida orchestrator-init after 10s`, so automation could not parse a JSON operator envelope.\n- Expected behavior from project documentation: AGENTS compact re-entry uses `vida orchestrator-init --json`; `docs/process/codex-agent-configuration-guide.md` requires `orchestrator-init --json` to expose machine-readable runtime contracts and fail closed for lock/contention; `docs/product/spec/orchestrator-runtime-contract-hardening-design.md` requires lock/contention style failures to return degraded operator-readable output; TaskFlow proof-runbook requires JSON operator contracts for every tested surface.\n\nArchitecture decision\n\n- Bounded code fix: `crates/vida/src/init_surfaces.rs`.\n- Keep successful startup behavior unchanged.\n- For the `build_taskflow_consume_bundle_payload` timeout branch, preserve plain text output for non-JSON mode, but emit a release-1 style JSON envelope when `--json` is requested.\n- The JSON envelope reports `status=blocked`, `blocker_codes=[taskflow_consume_bundle_timeout]`, actionable `next_actions`, `artifact_refs`, `operator_contracts`, and `shared_fields`.\n\nProof\n\n- `cargo test -p vida orchestrator_init_bundle_timeout_payload_is_json_operator_envelope -- --nocapture`: pass.\n- `cargo test -p vida orchestrator_init -- --nocapture`: pass, 6 matching tests.\n- `cargo fmt --check -p vida`: blocked by pre-existing unrelated formatter drift in files outside this bounded write scope; touched file was formatted through `cargo fmt -p vida -- crates/vida/src/init_surfaces.rs`, then unrelated formatter-only edits were reverted.\n- `cargo build -p vida --release`: pass.\n- `target\\release\\vida.exe release install --json`: pass.\n- `(Get-Command vida).Source` fingerprint equals `target\\release\\vida.exe`: true.\n- Live post-install proof: `vida orchestrator-init --json` now returns JSON with `status=blocked`, `blocker_codes=[taskflow_consume_bundle_timeout]`, `operator_contracts.status=blocked`, and `shared_fields.status=blocked`.\n","labels":["defect","operator-contract","orchestrator-init","remediation","taskflow-testing"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"sequential","order_bucket":"taskflow-testing-defects","parallel_group":"taskflow-testing-defects","conflict_domain":"taskflow-testing-runtime"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-defect-orchestrator-init-json-timeout-envelope","depends_on_id":"taskflow-testing-defects-epic","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1778675651296689