{"id":"taskflow-stale-blocked-run-retire-command-actionability","display_id":null,"title":"Fix stale blocked run retire command actionability","description":"Self-test after closing taskflow-closed-blocked-run-retire-actionability left latest run runtime-fix-closed-blocked-run-retire-actionability blocked against an already closed task. Status says reconcile or retire the stale blocked run, but taskflow run-graph/recovery help exposes no concrete retire/reconcile command, so the operator cannot lawfully clear the stale run before selecting the next bounded step. Add a concrete TaskFlow-local retire/reconcile operator path and diagnostics for closed-task blocked runs.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1778652905088603300","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1778656103238053500","closed_at":"1778656103238045300","close_reason":null,"source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"Implemented concrete closed-task stale-run retirement path: added vida lane retire, terminal run-graph status transition, continuation binding clear, receipt completion evidence, and state-store normalization for retired_closed_task_run lane_completed receipts. Proof: cargo test -p vida lane_retire_marks_closed_task_stale_run_terminal -- --nocapture; cargo test -p vida parse_lane_retire_supports_receipt_id_reason_and_json -- --nocapture; cargo test -p vida blocked_latest_run_graph_status_for_closed_task_is_retire_actionable -- --nocapture; git diff --check; cargo build -p vida --release; release install fingerprint verified.","labels":[],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":null,"order_bucket":null,"parallel_group":null,"conflict_domain":null},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[]}
{"id":"taskflow-test-program-case-catalog","display_id":null,"title":"TaskFlow complete test-case catalog","description":"Maintain the authoritative list of TaskFlow test cases, expected commands, expected outputs, defect-routing rules, and coverage gaps.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1778669182971656400","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1778674847005723300","closed_at":"1778674847005723300","close_reason":"case catalog completed: task notes contain the 21 TaskFlow case families with expected command surfaces, expected outputs, defect-routing rules, execution order, and project-doc expected-behavior sources","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"TaskFlow complete test-case catalog\n\nDate: 2026-05-13\nTask: `taskflow-test-program-case-catalog`\nLane: recovered local exception path after `internal_activation_view_only`\n\nExpected behavior source\n\n- `docs/process/team-development-and-orchestration-protocol.md`: activation/view-only without execution evidence is a bridge blocker, not delegated completion; open delegated state must be superseded before local recovery work.\n- `docs/process/project-orchestrator-operating-protocol.md`: internal host activation view is not execution evidence; bridge blockers require bounded diagnosis/recovery and explicit exception-path receipt before local mutation.\n- `docs/product/spec/canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md`: Layer 5 handoff/context governance requires explicit packets and bounded handoff evidence; Layer 7 recovery must be checkpoint/replay-safe and fail closed.\n- `docs/product/spec/canonical-runtime-readiness-law.md`: non-ready runtime consumption fails closed with explicit blockers.\n\nCatalog coverage rule\n\nEach case family below must record:\n\n1. setup/precondition,\n2. command surface under test,\n3. expected JSON/operator contract fields,\n4. expected failure mode when inputs are invalid,\n5. defect-routing rule when behavior diverges,\n6. proof command or evidence artifact.\n\nCase families\n\n1. `taskflow-case-bootstrap-orchestrator-init`\n   - Commands: `vida orchestrator-init --json`, `vida status --json`.\n   - Expected: active project/session evidence, no pending activation unless activation is genuinely incomplete, bounded next actions.\n   - Defect route: bootstrap/runtime-owner defects.\n\n2. `taskflow-case-task-lifecycle`\n   - Commands: `vida task ensure/show/update/close --json`.\n   - Expected: DB-backed task truth, dependency preservation, close reasons persisted.\n   - Defect route: task-store lifecycle defects.\n\n3. `taskflow-case-dependency-readiness`\n   - Commands: `vida task ready/next/validate-graph/critical-path --json`.\n   - Expected: blocked dependencies never appear as ready; graph invariants remain explicit.\n   - Defect route: dependency graph/readiness defects.\n\n4. `taskflow-case-continuation-binding`\n   - Commands: `vida taskflow continuation bind`, `vida taskflow next --json`.\n   - Expected: explicit bounded-unit binding; no heuristic `ready_head` selection without user/runtime evidence.\n   - Defect route: continuation ambiguity/actionability defects.\n\n5. `taskflow-case-run-graph-recovery`\n   - Commands: `vida taskflow run-graph status`, `vida taskflow recovery status`.\n   - Expected: lifecycle, active node, recovery readiness, and next action agree.\n   - Defect route: run-graph/recovery parity defects.\n\n6. `taskflow-case-consume-bundle-final`\n   - Commands: `vida taskflow consume bundle/check/final/continue --json`.\n   - Expected: direct consumption produces receipt-backed terminal or fail-closed blocker.\n   - Defect route: consume contract defects.\n\n7. `taskflow-case-lane-dispatch-agent-init`\n   - Commands: `vida agent-init --dispatch-packet ... --execute-dispatch --json`.\n   - Expected: activation view is not execution evidence; execution evidence must be receipt-backed.\n   - Defect route: dispatch execution/activation defects.\n\n8. `taskflow-case-lane-exception-takeover`\n   - Commands: `vida lane exception-takeover`, `vida lane show`.\n   - Expected: receipt states distinguish recorded, admissible, and active; root write scope remains bounded.\n   - Defect route: exception takeover state defects.\n\n9. `taskflow-case-lane-complete-fanout`\n   - Commands: `vida lane complete`.\n   - Expected: completion receipt transitions lane and downstream preview/fanout consistently.\n   - Defect route: lane completion/fanout defects.\n\n10. `taskflow-case-lane-supersede-activation`\n    - Commands: `vida lane supersede`, `vida lane show`.\n    - Expected: superseded exception lanes unblock delegated-cycle recovery only when receipt evidence is valid.\n    - Defect route: supersede/takeover activation defects.\n\n11. `taskflow-case-closure-admission`\n    - Commands: `vida task close`, `vida taskflow consume final`.\n    - Expected: closure requires task evidence, no open delegated cycle, and no missing proof gate.\n    - Defect route: closure admission defects.\n\n12. `taskflow-case-post-commit-diagnostics`\n    - Commands: `vida diagnostics post-commit --json`.\n    - Expected: git cleanliness, owner evidence, TaskFlow status, and latest run graph are reconciled.\n    - Defect route: diagnostics/actionability defects.\n\n13. `taskflow-case-orchestrator-session-owner`\n    - Commands: `vida orchestrator-session show --json`.\n    - Expected: no false `live_other_orchestrator_owner`; stale sessions reported as stale, not live.\n    - Defect route: session ownership defects.\n\n14. `taskflow-case-docflow-integration`\n    - Commands: `vida docflow readiness-check`, `vida docflow proofcheck`.\n    - Expected: docs/proofs are activated when runtime closure depends on documentation readiness.\n    - Defect route: DocFlow integration/readiness defects.\n\n15. `taskflow-case-release-install-fingerprint`\n    - Commands: `cargo build -p vida --release`, `target\\release\\vida.exe release install --json`, `Get-Command vida`.\n    - Expected: installed binary fingerprint matches `target\\release\\vida.exe`.\n    - Defect route: release install/fingerprint defects.\n\n16. `taskflow-case-datastore-lock-timeout`\n    - Commands: any TaskFlow mutation under lock contention.\n    - Expected: bounded timeout with actionable blocker; no silent stale mutation.\n    - Defect route: state-store lock defects.\n\n17. `taskflow-case-carrier-admissibility`\n    - Commands: runtime lane selection and dispatch preflight.\n    - Expected: selected backend is admissible for runtime role, task class, write scope, and readiness.\n    - Defect route: assignment/admissibility defects.\n\n18. `taskflow-case-json-operator-contracts`\n    - Commands: every public TaskFlow JSON surface.\n    - Expected: stable `status`, `blocker_codes`, `next_actions`, and `artifact_refs`.\n    - Defect route: operator contract schema defects.\n\n19. `taskflow-case-parallelism-conflicts`\n    - Commands: `vida taskflow parallelism`, `vida taskflow graph-summary`.\n    - Expected: conflict domains prevent unsafe parallel mutation and expose parallel-safe work clearly.\n    - Defect route: parallelism/conflict defects.\n\n20. `taskflow-case-export-import-snapshot`\n    - Commands: snapshot/export/import/degraded read surfaces.\n    - Expected: snapshots are fallback evidence only and never mistaken for live mutable authority.\n    - Defect route: snapshot authority defects.\n\n21. `taskflow-case-error-actionability`\n    - Commands: failing variants across TaskFlow surfaces.\n    - Expected: every blocker has a concrete, valid next action with target run/task/receipt evidence.\n    - Defect route: error actionability defects.\n\nExecution order\n\n1. Run bootstrap/session-owner/readiness cases first.\n2. Run task lifecycle and dependency cases.\n3. Run run-graph/consume/lane cases.\n4. Run diagnostics/release/fingerprint cases after each defect closure.\n5. Route every divergent behavior into `taskflow-testing-defects-epic` and fix it through the 1/3 -> 3/3 defect protocol with project-doc expected-behavior actualization.\n","labels":["program","taskflow-testing"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"sequential","order_bucket":"taskflow-testing-program","parallel_group":"taskflow-testing-program","conflict_domain":"taskflow-testing-program"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-test-program-case-catalog","depends_on_id":"taskflow-testing-program-epic","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1778669182971656400","created_by":"vida task","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
{"id":"taskflow-test-program-proof-runbook","display_id":null,"title":"TaskFlow testing proof runbook","description":"Define repeatable proof gates for each TaskFlow test case: targeted commands, release build/install/fingerprint, diagnostics, closure, commit, and push expectations.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1778669184384837600","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1778675339614660000","closed_at":"1778675339614660000","close_reason":"proof runbook completed: task notes define expected-behavior authorities, standard proof gates, per-case proof targets for all 21 TaskFlow case families, defect-routing protocol, release/install/fingerprint/diagnostics gates, and commit/push expectations","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"TaskFlow testing proof runbook\n\nExpected-behavior authority\n\n- Project documentation is the authority for agent behavior at all affected levels.\n- Required sources for each case: AGENTS.md, AGENTS.sidecar.md, docs/process/team-development-and-orchestration-protocol.md, docs/process/project-orchestrator-operating-protocol.md, docs/product/spec/canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md, docs/product/spec/canonical-runtime-readiness-law.md, and the case-specific command/operator contract.\n- Runtime code contracts and existing tests are supporting evidence only. If project docs and runtime behavior disagree, route a defect/spec clarification before implementing from intuition.\n\nStandard proof gate for every TaskFlow case\n\n1. Record the active bounded unit, why it is the current unit, and whether execution is sequential or parallel-safe.\n2. Capture clean starting state with `git status --short --branch`, task/run status, lane status, and relevant recovery/status JSON.\n3. Run the targeted command under test with `--json` when the surface supports it.\n4. Assert JSON/operator contract fields: `status`, `blocker_codes`, `next_actions`, `artifact_refs`, run id, task id, lane id, dispatch receipt, continuation binding, and recovery readiness when applicable.\n5. Compare observed behavior to expected behavior from the project docs and the command contract before deciding whether the case is pass, expected blocker, or defect.\n6. If a defect is found, create or update the defect task under `taskflow-testing-defects-epic`, then run the three-step defect cycle: `Крок 1/3: дослідження`, `Крок 2/3: архітектурне рішення + bounded write scope`, `Крок 3/3: code fix`.\n7. During `Крок 1/3`, after reading related/dependent code and before the fix decision, actualize expected behavior from project documentation for the affected agent/runtime/operator levels.\n8. Add or update targeted unit/contract tests for changed behavior.\n9. Run `cargo fmt --check -p vida`.\n10. Run targeted `cargo test -p vida ... -- --nocapture` proof for the changed surface. Broader tests that exceed the current tool window must be recorded as bounded proof-window risk, not as green evidence.\n11. Run `cargo build -p vida --release`.\n12. Run `target\\release\\vida.exe release install --json`.\n13. Verify `(Get-Command vida).Source` resolves to the installed release path and its fingerprint equals `target\\release\\vida.exe`.\n14. Run `vida diagnostics post-commit --json`.\n15. Close or retire the TaskFlow run only when its bounded task is complete and diagnostics do not report an unresolved blocker for that unit.\n16. If tracked source or instruction files changed, commit and push before selecting the next case. If only untracked runtime state changed, record that no git commit is required and continue.\n\nCase-family proof targets\n\n- `taskflow-case-bootstrap-orchestrator-init`: prove bounded init either returns ready JSON or a concrete operator blocker with actionable next commands.\n- `taskflow-case-task-lifecycle`: prove create/update/show/close state transitions preserve task identity, status, close reason, and parent links.\n- `taskflow-case-dependency-readiness`: prove blocked dependencies prevent premature execution and unblocked dependencies surface readiness.\n- `taskflow-case-continuation-binding`: prove active bounded unit, why-this-unit, and sequential/parallel posture are explicit before writes.\n- `taskflow-case-run-graph-recovery`: prove run graph status, recovery status, and consume continuation agree on concrete run id and recovery readiness.\n- `taskflow-case-consume-bundle-final`: prove final snapshots publish retrieval trust, release admission, artifact refs, and next actions.\n- `taskflow-case-lane-dispatch-agent-init`: prove delegated dispatch distinguishes execution evidence from activation/view-only bridges.\n- `taskflow-case-lane-exception-takeover`: prove receipt-recorded, admissible-not-active, and active states remain distinct and only active unlocks bounded root-local write.\n- `taskflow-case-lane-complete-fanout`: prove lane completion records receipt-backed downstream completion evidence and unblocks dependent transitions.\n- `taskflow-case-lane-supersede-activation`: prove supersede activates valid exception takeover when the recorded receipt and bounded unit match.\n- `taskflow-case-closure-admission`: prove closure is denied until task evidence, lane evidence, release gate, and diagnostics are complete.\n- `taskflow-case-post-commit-diagnostics`: prove diagnostics distinguish git dirty, open cycle, stale owner, missing dispatch receipt, and clean closure.\n- `taskflow-case-orchestrator-session-owner`: prove session-owner evidence reports current owner, stale owner, and competing owner without false clean pass.\n- `taskflow-case-docflow-integration`: prove documentation-shaped work routes through docflow/readiness/proof evidence when docs are the authority.\n- `taskflow-case-release-install-fingerprint`: prove release build, install, path resolution, and fingerprint equality before continued testing.\n- `taskflow-case-datastore-lock-timeout`: prove store lock contention reports bounded actionable blockers rather than silent hang.\n- `taskflow-case-carrier-admissibility`: prove carrier selection uses configured catalogs and readiness, not hardcoded host templates.\n- `taskflow-case-json-operator-contracts`: prove every operator surface used in TaskFlow emits stable JSON fields for automation.\n- `taskflow-case-parallelism-conflicts`: prove conflicting bounded units are sequentialized and independent units remain parallel-safe.\n- `taskflow-case-export-import-snapshot`: prove snapshot export/import preserves task ids, dependencies, labels, status, notes, and receipts.\n- `taskflow-case-error-actionability`: prove every blocker includes the failing surface, concrete target, reason, and next lawful command.\n\nExecution order\n\nRun the cases in the listed order unless runtime readiness or a newly found defect makes a later case the direct blocker for the current bounded unit. Defect fixes may interrupt the case order only after the defect has been recorded under the defect epic and the active bounded unit has been restated.\n","labels":["program","taskflow-testing"],"execution_semantics":{"execution_mode":"sequential","order_bucket":"taskflow-testing-program","parallel_group":"taskflow-testing-program","conflict_domain":"taskflow-testing-program"},"planner_metadata":{"owned_paths":[],"acceptance_targets":[],"proof_targets":[],"risk":null,"estimate":null,"lane_hint":null},"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"taskflow-test-program-proof-runbook","depends_on_id":"taskflow-testing-program-epic","edge_type":"parent-child","created_at":"1778669184384837600","created_by":"vida task","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
{"id":"taskflow-test-program-scope-matrix","display_id":null,"title":"TaskFlow testing scope and surface matrix","description":"Map all TaskFlow surfaces, commands, state stores, run-graph/lane/continuation/diagnostic contracts, and define coverage ownership for the full testing program.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"1778669181274086200","created_by":"vida task","updated_at":"1778672966663460700","closed_at":"1778672966663460700","close_reason":"scope matrix completed: task notes contain the TaskFlow surface/state/contract ownership matrix and follow-on binding for case catalog and proof runbook; delegated lane recovered via exception takeover and completed","source_repo":"C:\\project\\vida-stack","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"notes":"TaskFlow testing scope and surface matrix\n\nDate: 2026-05-13\nTask: `taskflow-test-program-scope-matrix`\nLane: delegated `pm`\nPacket target: `specification`\n\nSummary\n\n- This task defines the canonical coverage map for the TaskFlow testing program.\n- The matrix is scoped to TaskFlow runtime-family surfaces and the adjacent `vida task` backlog contract that TaskFlow owns.\n- Coverage ownership is split across the three program tasks:\n  - `taskflow-test-program-scope-matrix`: maintain the surface inventory, command families, state-store boundaries, and contract-to-test ownership.\n  - `taskflow-test-program-case-catalog`: expand each scoped surface into concrete test cases, commands, expected outputs, and defect-routing rules.\n  - `taskflow-test-program-proof-runbook`: define the repeatable proof sequence for each case, including build/install/fingerprint/diagnostic/closure expectations.\n\nCommand surface matrix\n\n| Surface family | Canonical commands | What must be covered |\n|---|---|---|\n| Backlog contract | `vida task list/show/progress/ready/next/next-lawful/create/update/deps/children/tree/validate-graph/critical-path/owned-status/handoff/close/split/spawn-blocker` | authoritative task truth, graph mutations, notes/proof persistence, dependency integrity, and owned-path reporting |\n| Runtime family entry | `vida taskflow help`, `vida taskflow query`, `vida taskflow status` | command discovery, family routing, fail-closed operator guidance |\n| Queue and ordering | `vida taskflow queue`, `vida taskflow next`, `vida taskflow graph`, `vida taskflow graph-summary`, `vida taskflow parallelism`, `vida taskflow dependencies` | ready/blocked posture, sequencing, lawful parallelism, and critical-path reasoning |\n| Planning and adaptive reshaping | `vida taskflow plan`, `vida taskflow replan`, `vida taskflow scheduler` | deterministic draft generation, split/spawn-blocker previews, lane-selection preview integrity |\n| Packet and artifact inspection | `vida taskflow continuation`, `vida taskflow packet`, `vida taskflow artifacts` | bounded-unit binding, dispatch-packet truth, required artifact readiness, and resume inputs |\n| Run execution state | `vida taskflow run-graph`, `vida taskflow recovery`, `vida taskflow consume` | run lifecycle, resumability, downstream continuation, checkpoint/recovery truth |\n| Bootstrap and protocol bridge | `vida taskflow bootstrap-spec`, `vida taskflow protocol-binding` | design-first bootstrap correctness and protocol/runtime bridge receipts |\n\nState-store and artifact matrix\n\n| Store / path class | Observed role | Coverage expectation |\n|---|---|---|\n| authoritative backlog store behind `vida task` | source of truth for tasks and dependency graph | command correctness, graph integrity, notes/proof persistence |\n| `.vida/data/state/runtime-consumption/dispatch-packets/` | persisted dispatch packet evidence | packet render fidelity, scope/read-scope correctness, activation vs execution distinction |\n| `.vida/data/state/runtime-consumption/dispatch-results/` | delegated execution results | receipt classification, execution evidence availability, downstream dispatch gating |\n| `.vida/data/state/runtime-consumption/downstream-dispatch-packets/` | follow-on packet preparation | continuation truth and lawful downstream admission |\n| `.vida/exports/tasks.snapshot.jsonl` | degraded read-side snapshot fallback, not live authority | snapshot fallback behavior must remain explicit and never be mistaken for live mutable state |\n\nContract and ownership matrix\n\n| Area | Canonical law / evidence | Testing ownership |\n|---|---|---|\n| lane routing and assignment | `docs/product/spec/canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md` Layer 4; `vida taskflow help` command homes | scope-matrix task defines coverage boundary; case catalog enumerates route-selection cases |\n| handoff/context governance | `canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md` Layer 5; packet surfaces from `vida taskflow packet` | scope-matrix task defines artifact/state coverage; proof runbook defines receipt checks |\n| specification-lane scope | `docs/product/spec/specification-lane-scope-hardening-design.md` | case catalog must include doc-only scope assertions for `specification` packets |\n| run-graph completion vs diagnostic execution | `docs/product/spec/analysis-lane-can-close-implementation-without-write-evidence-design.md` | case catalog must include negative completion/closure cases for diagnostic-only execution |\n| resumability and recovery | `canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md` Layer 7; `vida taskflow run-graph/recovery` | case catalog enumerates interruption/resume cases; proof runbook defines replay/recovery proof sequence |\n| observability and readiness | `canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md` Layer 8; `vida taskflow status`; `vida docflow` readiness/proof surfaces when docs are touched | proof runbook owns readiness and diagnostic proof gates |\n| direct runtime consumption boundary | `canonical-runtime-layer-matrix.md` Layer 9; `vida taskflow consume` | case catalog and proof runbook cover lawful continue/final/advance behavior |\n\nCurrent packet-specific evidence\n\n- `vida task show taskflow-test-program-sc